  "summary": "Monday 10/26 CT list at St. Brigid Imaging (7 bookings) is ready under RBC-RAD-07. Six studies are ordered and linked to their appointments. One contrast scan is not ordered: Schmitt, below. Every patient has written instructions, and each chart has a note.\n\n- **Mohr (pt-0047), 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0001):** Has diabetes, and his last creatinine (09/24) is more than 30 days old. Ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0007). No premedication needed.\n- **Ferreira (pt-0015), 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0002):** The 2019 radiology report grades his iohexol reaction as moderate. His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\", but per policy that doesn't change the grade. Prescribed the premedication:\n  - Prednisone 50 mg Sun 20:00, Mon 02:00 and Mon 08:00 (mr-t0010).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg Mon 08:00 (mr-t0011).\n  - He has been told he must not drive and needs a driver.\n  - His 10/14 creatinine (0.98) is normal, so no other prep.\n- **Stracke (pt-0012), 11:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0003):** Has stage 3 kidney disease; creatinine was 2.85 on 10/13, giving an eGFR of 24.5. That is not acute kidney injury and he is not on dialysis. Ordered 500 mL IV saline starting at 10:00 (mr-t0012). He is not on metformin. He was told to arrive by 10:00.\n- **Schuster (pt-0049), 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0004):** Had acute kidney injury in the ED on 10/04; creatinine was still not back to baseline at discharge and hasn't been checked since.\n  - Ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0008).\n  - Ordered 500 mL IV saline at 12:00 (mr-t0013).\n  - Put metformin on hold now (mr-00392), through 48 hours after the scan. A task (task-t0026) is set to recheck kidney function before restarting it.\n- **Beahan (pt-0046), 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0005):** No prep needed; she was told so.\n- **Brakus (pt-0050), 15:00, CT abdomen with contrast, adrenal protocol (sr-t0006):** Has acute kidney injury: creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 between 10/19 and 10/21, after ibuprofen and vomiting.\n  - Ordered a new creatinine before the scan (sr-t0009).\n  - Ordered 500 mL IV saline at 14:00 (mr-t0014).\n  - Put metformin on hold now (mr-00398), through 48 hours after the scan. A restart task (task-t0027) is set.\n- **Schmitt (pt-0048), 10:00, contrast CT — not ordered:** The 2023 radiology report documents a severe reaction to contrast (anaphylaxis with low blood pressure and wheezing, treated with epinephrine). Per §3 I placed no contrast order, no substitute study and no premedication.\n  - I messaged the radiologist, Dr. Adeyemi (comm-t0017), to decide what is done instead.\n  - His allergy entry (alg-00025) said \"mild hives\"; I updated it to severe, citing the radiology report.\n  - He was told to take no premedication and that he'll be contacted about the plan.\n\n**Your follow-up:**\n- An urgent task due today (task-t0028) is yours: once Dr. Adeyemi replies, place whatever order he decides on and let Mr. Schmitt know.\n- The three patients needing creatinine must have blood drawn before their Monday scan times. The radiologist reviews the results on the day; the scans are not delayed for them.",
